  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Sustainable and Socially Inclusive Labour Market Integration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 48-month project aims to increase formal employment of Syrians under Temporary Protection, Persons under International Protection and host community members and harmonization process in T&#xfc;rkiye. T&#xfc;rkiye hosts the largest refugee population in the world. According to the statistics of the Presidency of the Migration Management of the Ministry of Interior (PMM), as of August 2023, there are over 4.8 million foreign nationals living in T&#xfc;rkiye, approximately 3.3 million of them being Syrians registered under temporary protection, accounting for more than 4 per cent of T&#xfc;rkiye&#x2019;s population. In addition, an estimated 337,000 international protection holders and applicants, mainly from Iraq, Afghanistan and the Islamic Republic of Iran, reside in the country. Given the considerable size of the community of people under protection as well as regular migrants, providing means for their social and economic integration is a very challenging process for both, national as well as local authorities. The proposed Action will propose a two-prong approach that will ensure that targeted populations have improved levels of employability and access to social protection services and are better integrated in their host communities. This will be done by strengthening the institutional capacities at the national as much as provincial level for delivering efficient employability and integration services for the targeted populations. In doing so, IOM will build on lessons learned from previous and ongoing projects.</narrative>
  </description>
